t with the  virus look at  there's other examples it was really  good for the leaders  and had trump at the beginning thought  hey  forget about the fact that he doesn't  care about people he never cared about  people  but if trump had said at the beginning  the best thing politically for me  is to manage this virus by doing a ton  of testing which helps people identify  if they're sick and stay home and not  spread the virus if he had done that it  would have been good for him politically  and as i've said many many times before  if donald trump had just done a passably  okay job on the virus  he would be president right now instead  of joe biden there's no question about  that whatsoever  but instead trump's concern was  sabotaging the spread of the virus  containment aspect in order to do what  he believed but  wrongly so that would look good and in  the end  it didn't help it actually was a  complete and total disaster  just a couple of other things here trump  and his aides belittled and resisted  life-saving public health measures  obviously  the book reports that mark short a  veteran trump aide serving as  pence's chief of staff opposed a plan  to send free masks to every household on  the grounds that it would alarm the  public  senior trump officials ridiculed masks  likening them to a training bra  or underwear on your face short also  opposed the economic shutdown that  slowed the spread of the virus in march  and april  and on the rare occasions when trump  pushed subordinates to move more quickly  he did so for personal advantage  not public health in the fall according  to the book  he tried to oust fda commissioner  stephen hahn  for refusing to strong-arm fda  scientists into approving coveted  vaccines  before election day one anecdote  reported in the book  is more significant than it might seem  in late march of 2020 robert cadillac a  senior hhs official  went to trump's senior advisor and  son-in-law jared kushner  with a plan to mass distribute masks  when kushner learned the masks wouldn't  arrive until june he exploded  we'll all be dead by june he told  cadillac in the post's retelling  this conversation comes across as a tale  of delay and frustration  but it's worse than that it shows how  gravely kushner and others in the white  house privately viewed the crisis  which trump was telling americans  publicly the virus would soon disappear  that is the epitome and a microcosm of  the entire handling of the virus  we learned from the bob woodward  interview that trump did trump knew it  was more serious than he was letting on  he said he didn't want to scare people  jared kushner based on this anecdote  clearly knew  privately how serious it was uh  everything  that they did was based on their worst  instincts their most self-centered  instincts and a complete and total  lack of empathy and concern i mean just  a disgusting  expose no individual incident is  particularly shocking  because what was going on publicly was  bad enough but i believe that we will  continue to learn more about this just  about every week  we're learning more about what was going  on and it's as disgusting as you can  imagine
 

